WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Hydrogen enters a cooled metal-hydride reactor and is absorbed into the solid bed, releasing heat.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:16.000
The bed warms until absorption stalls near its equilibrium temperature. Heat removed through the jacketed wall lets the reaction continue.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:26.500
The reacted fraction advances as a front from the cooled wall toward the hot core of the bed.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Supply pressure and coolant temperature set the charging time. These trade-offs guide safer, faster reactor design.
